# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Gets the dates of an act, the dates of every act that its consolidations integrate, and the dates
# of every act that amends it, for CellarDates. An act that amends it can be in no consolidation
# yet. It gets two kinds of dates, and ?property tells which:
# - Each date of entry into force as Cellar has it, with the annotations that type the date:
#   - The type of date, from the authority table fd_335. EV is entry into force, MA is application
#     and PE is taking effect. /PART means that the date applies to part of the act.
#   - Cellar's comment on the date. For example, "DATPUB +20 V ART 2" means 20 days after
#     publication, see Article 2. "ET 32020R0910" names a later act: one that amended the date, or
#     one that set a day that the clause left to it.
#   - ?amending: the acts that the comment names and that amend the act of the date, by their CELEX
#     numbers, with a space between them. Cellar's comment is the same for an act that amended the
#     date and for an act that set it. An act that amends the act of the date amended the date: for
#     example, 2020/910 replaces "31 December 2020" in Article 2 of 2019/103. A named act that does
#     not amend it set the day: Decision 2023/201 sets the day from which 2018/1862 applies.
# - Each date of transposition of a directive. It has no type. Its comment starts with a code from
#   the authority table fd_361: APPLICATION is the day from which the Member States apply their
#   measures, and ADOPTION is the day by which they adopt them.
# The consolidations also list earlier consolidations. These have dates but no annotations, and
# CellarDates leaves them out.
# It uses consolidations with or without a CELEX number: internal production versions name acts
# that a public consolidation left out. CellarActs retains only dates of acts that a version in the
# act's timeline integrates, or that amend the act.
# It gives one row per date and annotation.
# {{celex}}: the CELEX number of the base act, for example 32015R1998. Sparql.fill escapes it.
PREFIX cdm: <http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/cdm#>
PREFIX annotation: <http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/annotation#>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>

SELECT ?subject ?property ?date ?type ?comment
  (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?amender; separator=" ") AS ?amending)
WHERE {
  {
    ?work cdm:resource_legal_id_celex "{{celex}}"^^xsd:string .
  } UNION {
    ?act cdm:resource_legal_id_celex "{{celex}}"^^xsd:string .
    ?consolidation cdm:act_consolidated_based_on_resource_legal ?act ;
         cdm:act_consolidated_consolidates_resource_legal ?work .
  } UNION {
    ?act cdm:resource_legal_id_celex "{{celex}}"^^xsd:string .
    ?work cdm:resource_legal_amends_resource_legal ?act .
  }
  VALUES ?property { cdm:resource_legal_date_entry-into-force cdm:directive_date_transposition }
  ?work cdm:resource_legal_id_celex ?subject ;
       ?property ?date .
  OPTIONAL {
    ?axiom owl:annotatedSource ?work ;
         owl:annotatedProperty ?property ;
         owl:annotatedTarget ?date .
    OPTIONAL { ?axiom annotation:type_of_date ?type }
    OPTIONAL { ?axiom annotation:comment_on_date ?comment }
  }
  OPTIONAL {
    ?amenderWork cdm:resource_legal_amends_resource_legal ?work ;
         cdm:resource_legal_id_celex ?amender .
    FILTER (CONTAINS(STR(?comment), STR(?amender)))
  }
}
GROUP BY ?subject ?property ?date ?type ?comment
ORDER BY ?subject ?date
